Q1: 
You are designing a table for an e-commerce system
Choose appropriate datatypes for: - Order ID - Price (accurate to 2 decimal places) - Customer phone number - Order date

 Field                     Datatype                                 Why                                         
 Order ID     | INT (or BIGINT) + AUTO_INCREMENT | Unique numeric identifier, fast indexing          
 Price        | DECIMAL(10,2)                      | Exact precision (no floating error)               
 Phone number | VARCHAR(15)                        | Not used for math, may include country code (+91) 
 Order date   | DATE` or DATETIME                 | Stores date (and optionally time)                 

Q2:  Difference between CHAR and VARCHAR — give a real-world scenario where each is used 
CHAR                  | VARCHAR         
 Fixed length          | Variable length 
 Faster for fixed data | Saves space     
 Pads spaces           | No padding      
CHAR(2) - Country code (IN, US)
VARCHAR(100) - Customer name
=> CHAR is used when length is fixed, while VARCHAR is used when length varies to optimize storage

